{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.745, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:24.542Z", "t_ms": 6630, "delta": "### Contribution\nThe ReAct paper explores combining reasoning and acting in large language models"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.9, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:24.761Z", "t_ms": 6849, "delta": " (LLMs) in an interleaved manner [C1]. While prior work studied reasoning (e.g., chain-"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.113, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:24.975Z", "t_ms": 7063, "delta": "of-thought prompting) and acting (e.g., action plan generation) separately, ReAct enables reasoning traces to guide,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.312, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:25.173Z", "t_ms": 7260, "delta": " track, and update action plans, while allowing domain-specific actions to interface with external environments or knowledge sources [C1]. This"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.559, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:25.419Z", "t_ms": 7507, "delta": " synergy improves task success, grounds trajectories in factual information, and enhances human interpretability and controllability [C1, C3]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.831, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:25.691Z", "t_ms": 7779, "delta": "\n\n### Method\n* **Augmented Action Space:** ReAct expands an agent's action space to include a free"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.064, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:25.925Z", "t_ms": 8012, "delta": "-form language space ($\\mathcal{\\hat{A}} = \\mathcal{A} \\cup \\mathcal{L}$) ["}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.265, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:26.125Z", "t_ms": 8213, "delta": "C2]. Actions in $\\mathcal{L}$ represent internal reasoning traces or \"thoughts\" that do not affect the external environment"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.468, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:26.330Z", "t_ms": 8417, "delta": " or yield observation feedback, but update the internal context to assist future reasoning and planning [C2].\n* **Execution Format:** For"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.634, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:26.491Z", "t_ms": 8579, "delta": " reasoning-heavy tasks, thoughts and actions alternate strictly into thought-action-observation cycles [C3]. For decision-making tasks"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.819, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:26.680Z", "t_ms": 8768, "delta": " over long horizons, thoughts appear sparsely and asynchronously whenever needed (e.g., decomposing goals or tracking progress) [C2"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.007, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:26.867Z", "t_ms": 8955, "delta": ", C3].\n* **Implementation:** The authors primarily evaluate frozen PaLM-540B prompted with 1–6"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.227, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:27.088Z", "t_ms": 9176, "delta": " few-shot in-context trajectories containing human-written thoughts, actions, and observations [C1, C3]. They"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.43, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:27.287Z", "t_ms": 9375, "delta": " also evaluate fine-tuning PaLM-8B and PaLM-62B models using ReAct trajectories [C6].\n\n###"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.569, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:27.418Z", "t_ms": 9506, "delta": " Results\n* **Knowledge-Intensive Tasks (HotpotQA & Fever):** PaLM-540B prompted"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.832, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:27.692Z", "t_ms": 9780, "delta": " with ReAct outperforms an action-only baseline (Act) on both HotpotQA (27.4 vs. 25.7"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.963, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 43, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:27.825Z", "t_ms": 9912, "delta": " EM) and Fever (60.9 vs. 58.9 accuracy) by interacting with an external Wikipedia API"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.091, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 44, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:27.949Z", "t_ms": 10037, "delta": " [C1, C4]. While ReAct slightly lags behind Chain-of-Thought (CoT) on Hotpot"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.287, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 45, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:28.149Z", "t_ms": 10236, "delta": "QA (27.4 vs. 29.4), combining both methods (ReAct $\\to$ CoT-SC"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.42, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 46, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:28.281Z", "t_ms": 10369, "delta": " or CoT-SC $\\to$ ReAct) achieves the highest scores (35.1 and 64"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.585, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 47, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:28.447Z", "t_ms": 10535, "delta": ".6, respectively) [C4, C6].\n* **Fine-Tuning Scaling:** When fine-tuned on 3,"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.799, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 48, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:28.660Z", "t_ms": 10748, "delta": "000 examples on HotpotQA, ReAct becomes the best-performing method; fine-tuned PaLM-8"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 10.932, "data": {"request_id": "950a4689ebfa", "seq": 49, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:28.793Z", "t_ms": 10881, "delta": "B ReAct outperforms all PaLM-62B prompting methods, and fine-tuned PaLM-62B ReAct outperforms all"}}
